683 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1686 0 R
/E ( Expert Bias       | Weight: +4.0 A binary flag indicating if trained media experts explicitly labeled the text as biased. If experts agree it is biased, it mathematically guarantees a high severity score.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
684 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1687 0 R
/E ( Opinion/Subjectivity      | Max Weight: +3.0 A tiered multiplier based on the expert's classification of how the information is presented . "Entirely factual" = +0.0 \(No penalty, purely objective\). "Somewhat factual but also opinionated" = +1.5 \(Partial penalty for mixing facts with subjective framing\). "Expresses writer's opinion" = +3.0 \(Maximum penalty for entirely subjective claims masked as news\).)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
685 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1688 0 R
/E ( Lexical Density             | Weight: +2.0 The ratio of loaded/biased words to the total length of the sentence. A short sentence packed with slanted words gets a higher intensity penalty than a long paragraph with a single loaded word.)
/Pg 34 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
